  {
   "id": "intro",
   "texto": "This secretary died with seven million, two hundred thousand dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "who",
   "texto": "Grace Groner bought three shares for one hundred and eighty dollars, in nineteen thirty-five."
  },
  {
   "id": "how",
   "texto": "Then she did the hardest thing in investing. Nothing. Every dividend went back into more shares."
  },
  {
   "id": "payoff",
   "texto": "Seventy-five years later, three shares had become a fortune."
  },
  {
   "id": "honesty",
   "texto": "Here's the uncomfortable part. She could have sold any year she wanted. That's not a strategy. It's a trade almost nobody can make."
  },
  {
   "id": "lesson",
   "texto": "Own it, reinvest it, and leave it alone."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "texto": "Could you sit on a hundred and eighty dollars for seventy-five years?"
  }
 ],
